<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n111661" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φῑμ-ός</span></b> , ὁ, heterocl.
		pl. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φῑμά</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					6.312
				</span></i>
			 (<span class="entity">Anyte</span>):—<i>any instrument
				for keeping the mouth closed</i>: </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>I.</b>
			<i>muzzle,</i> for dogs, calves, etc., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φιμὸν περιτιθέναι τινί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Luc.
					<u>Vit.Auct.</u>
					22
				</span></i>
			, cf. <u>AP</u>l. c., <i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>Si.</u>
				20.29
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>gag</i>: hence, <i>silencing</i> by a spell, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Tab.Defix.Aud.</u>
				25.13
			</span></i> (Curium, <span class="entity">iii A. D.</span>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>nose-band</i> of a horse's bridle, fitted with pipes, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φ. δὲ συρίζουσι βάρβαρον βρόμον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Th.</u>
					463
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πώλους . . φιμοῖσιν αὐλωτοῖσιν
					ἐστομωμένας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					326
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐμβαλῶ φ. εἰς τὴν ῥῖνά σου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					LXX
					<u>Is.</u>
					37.29
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b> a kind of
				<i>cup,</i> used as <i>a dice-box,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Aeschin.
				1.59
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Diph.
				76
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				7.203
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				10.150
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>IV.</b>
			<i>tightening, constriction</i> by means of ropes, Apollod <i><span class="en">
				<u>Poliorc.</u>
				161.1
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>V.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φίμωσις</span>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				11.2
			</span></i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φ. τοὺς ἐν αἰδοίοις χαλᾷ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Dsc.
					4.91
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Androm.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				13.311
			</span></i>; <i>imperforation</i> of the anus, <i><span class="en">
				Heliod.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Orib.
				44.20.72
			</span></i>. (Connected with <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σφίγγω,
			σφιγμός</span> by <i><span class="en">
				<u>EM</u>
				795.21
			</span></i>.)</div>
